T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2025-12-08","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i20251208-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i20251208","date":"2025-12-08","original_code":"746.3701","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-12-15","finding":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards: One of the playgrounds has play equipment with exposed nails. Additionally, there is fake grass that is used as decoration on the play surface of the climbing equipment that is not tacked down and presents a tripping hazard. Pieces of lattice decoration are also loose that was previously nailed down that could present a pinch hazard. Inside the operation, the main office has prescription medication on the counter that children could reach if they were in the office. Upon arrival at the operation, a child was in the office, and the staff were attempting to help the child lay down for nap in the office.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026420579","violation_type_title":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards (26 TAC §746.3701)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i20251208-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3505-e","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i20251208","date":"2025-12-08","original_code":"746.3505(e)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-12-15","finding":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area: A caregiver was observed doing diaper changes and the diaper changing surface was not sanitized after each diaper change.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026460558","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area (26 TAC §746.3505(e))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i20251208-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3415-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-754968-i2